 "evidence": "chr_catalog descriptor +5 is the animation count and +16 points at a directory of that many u32 script pointers, the scripts sitting immediately before it. A script is (frame, duration) byte pairs, duration in 60Hz ticks, terminated by an opcode byte >= 0xf0 with one argument: 0xf1 hold, 0xfd and 0xfe loop. Decoded across the whole table this reads 5,692 frame references with 10 out of range, all in six banks whose extraction is short.",
 "gif_rule": "animation 1 is the idle loop and is what the gif shows. Animation 0 is a single-frame static pose in every bank checked; animation 1 holds one frame for 80-190 ticks and cuts to a second for 6-8, which is a blink or a breath, and ends on a loop opcode. Banks whose animation 1 has fewer than two steps fall back to the longest looping animation.",
